{"format":1,"key":"zone:dunmorogh","path":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh","name":"Dun Morogh","kind":"zone","label":"Zone","zone":{"key":"dunmorogh","name":"Dun Morogh","path":"/lore/zone/dunmorogh"},"levels":"Levels 1-10","description":"Dun Morogh is a snow-swept mountain highland situated at the heart of Khaz Modan. It serves as the ancestral starting ground and shared homeland for the…","intro":[],"clips":[{"id":"zone:dunmorogh","part":"narration","anchor":"story","title":"The story","paras":["Dun Morogh is a snow-swept mountain highland situated at the heart of Khaz Modan. It serves as the ancestral starting ground and shared homeland for the dwarves of Ironforge and the displaced gnomes of Gnomeregan. Though guarded by towering peaks and fortified passes, the snowy realm faces rising internal threats from troggs, Frostmane trolls, and irradiated leper gnomes.","Dun Morogh occupies the highest peaks in the Eastern Kingdoms, an alpine expanse ringed by jagged summits that shield it from Searing Gorge to the south and the Wetlands to the north. These snowy mountains feed the rivers flowing across Khaz Modan and provide near-limitless veins of copper and iron. Access is heavily restricted to mountain tunnels like North Gate Pass and South Gate Pass, watched closely by dwarven Mountaineers. At the heart of the region sits Ironforge, an ancient subterranean wonder and the capital of King Magni Bronzebeard's realm, linked straight to Stormwind by the marvel of the Deeprun Tram.","Centuries ago, the dwarves drove the native Frostmane ice trolls into the crags, carving out room for themselves alongside their brilliant gnome allies. The two races flourished in neighboring mountain halls until the recent catastrophe in Gnomeregan during the Third War. A horrific trogg invasion and a catastrophic radioactive venting ruined the technological wonder, turning its defenders into mindless leper gnomes and driving High Tinker Gelbin Mekkatorque and his surviving folk into exile. Now, the gnomes dwell as guests inside Ironforge, while leper gnomes and surviving troggs spill out into Chill Breeze Valley.","Life in the drifts is far from quiet. The Frostmane tribe has grown emboldened, establishing heavily armed encampments from Shimmer Ridge down to Coldridge Valley. Meanwhile, primitive troggs have clawed their way out of ancient subterranean fissures into Gol'Bolar Quarry, threatening the region's mining operations. Between prowling wendigos, wild boars, infiltrating Dark Iron dwarven agents, and toxic fallout spreading from the ruins of Gnomeregan, the dwarven Mountaineers are stretched thin maintaining order from Kharanos to the border gates."],"hash":"b44509","voices":{"male-narrator":{"sha":"c928e74831","sec":128},"female-narrator":{"sha":"79f74bcc1b","sec":136}}}],"sources":[{"kind":"wiki","title":"Dun Morogh (Classic)","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dun_Morogh_(Classic)"},{"kind":"wiki","title":"Dun Morogh","url":"https://warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Dun_Morogh"}],"related":[{"p":"/lore/zone/ironforge","n":"Ironforge","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/zone/gnomeregan","n":"Gnomeregan","k":"dungeon"},{"p":"/lore/zone/lochmodan","n":"Loch Modan","k":"zone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/kharanos","n":"Kharanos","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/coldridge-valley","n":"Coldridge Valley","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/deeprun-tram","n":"Deeprun Tram","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/gol-bolar-quarry","n":"Gol'Bolar Quarry","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/anvilmar","n":"Anvilmar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/item/tough-wolf-meat","n":"Tough Wolf Meat","k":"item"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/amberstill-ranch","n":"Amberstill Ranch","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/brewnall-village","n":"Brewnall Village","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/chill-breeze-valley","n":"Chill Breeze Valley","k":"subzone"}],"children":[{"p":"/lore/subzone/amberstill-ranch","n":"Amberstill Ranch","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/anvilmar","n":"Anvilmar","k":"subzone"},{"p":"/lore/subzone/br